Imports:
  - Types:
      - Backend
    From: server/storage/backend
  - Types:
      - Lessor
    From: server/lease

Usages:
  watch_sync_states: |
    Registered watchers live in one of two groups: "synced" (caught up to the store's current
    revision, receiving events live as they are committed) and "unsynced" (behind, being
    replayed from history in the background). A watcher whose delivery channel is full becomes
    a "victim" and is retried separately rather than blocking the writer that produced the
    event. New watch-related logic should preserve this three-way split rather than assuming a
    single delivery path.

Annotations: |
  This cell implements etcd's multi-version concurrency control key-value layer on top of the
  imported `Backend`: the monotonically increasing revision counter, the in-memory index
  mapping user keys to their revision history, compaction, consistency hashing, and the watch
  subsystem that turns committed writes into a stream of change events. It depends on `Backend`
  for physical storage and on `Lessor` so that Put operations can attach a key to a lease and
  so lease-driven key deletion can be wired in without this cell depending on the lease cell's
  internals.

  Use `watch_sync_states` when extending watch delivery or resync behavior.

---

"KV()":
  location: kv.go
  annotations: |
    The core read/write contract: point-in-time reads and transactional writes over the
    revisioned key space.
  methods:
    "Range(key []byte, end []byte) -> result:RangeResult, err:error": |
      Read the current (or a historical) value(s) for `key`, or for the range up to (excluding)
      `end` if `end` is set.
    "Put(key []byte, value []byte, leaseID int64) -> revision:int64": |
      Write `value` at `key`, creating a new revision; if `leaseID` is non-zero, attach the key
      to that lease via the imported `Lessor`.
    "DeleteRange(key []byte, end []byte) -> deleted:int64, revision:int64": |
      Delete `key`, or every key from `key` up to (excluding) `end`, creating a new tombstone
      revision.
    "Read(mode ReadTxMode) -> transaction:TxnRead": |
      Begin a read-only transaction; `mode` selects between the shared read view and a
      non-blocking concurrent read view.
    "Write() -> transaction:TxnWrite": |
      Begin a read/write transaction spanning one raft-applied request.
    "Compact(revision int64) -> err:error": |
      Discard all revisions of all keys created before `revision`; completion is signalled
      asynchronously in the real implementation.
    "Restore(be Backend) -> err:error": |
      Rebuild in-memory state (index, watchers) from `be` after a snapshot has replaced the
      backend wholesale.
    "Close() -> err:error": |
      Stop background compaction/watch goroutines and release resources.

"KV::WatchableKV()":
  location: kv.go
  annotations: |
    A `KV` that can also be watched: every mutation applied through it is turned into change
    events for subscribed watch streams.
  methods:
    "NewWatchStream() -> stream:WatchStream": |
      Create a new independent stream on which one or more key ranges can be watched.

"WatchStream()":
  location: watcher.go
  annotations: |
    One consumer's set of active watches and the channel of resulting events; owned by a single
    caller (typically one gRPC watch stream) for its lifetime.
  methods:
    "Watch(id int64, key []byte, end []byte, startRevision int64) -> watchID:int64, err:error": |
      Begin watching `key` (or the range up to (excluding) `end`) starting from
      `startRevision`, classified per `watch_sync_states` based on how far behind
      `startRevision` is from the current revision.
    "Cancel(id int64) -> err:error": |
      Stop watching and release the resources for a previously registered watch.
    "RequestProgress(id int64)": |
      Ask for a progress notification on this watch even absent matching events.

"New(be Backend, lessor Lessor, cfg StoreConfig) -> kv:WatchableKV":
  location: watchable_store.go
  annotations: |
    Construct the MVCC store: creates the on-`Backend` bucket layout if absent, rebuilds the
    in-memory revision index from existing data, and wires itself into `lessor` so that
    lease expiry/revocation deletes the keys it owns.

    `be`: imported `Backend` this store persists to.
    `lessor`: imported `Lessor` this store attaches Put'd keys to and registers a key-deletion
    callback with.
    `cfg`: compaction batch size and pacing.

